# Soul Enervation's "Whenever one or more creature cards leave your graveyard, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life." Bot1
# casts the Enervation on turn 1 (no creature on the battlefield, so its enters ability has no target) and then Faithless Looting,
# which discards its Memnite and Ornithopter. On turn 2 Bot2's Tormod's Crypt exiles Bot1's whole graveyard at once - the two creature
# cards and the Looting - which is one batch (CR 603.2c: "one or more"): the drain happens exactly once, Bot2 at 19 and Bot1 at 21
# (a trigger for each card would leave 18 and 22).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Soul Enervation
Faithless Looting
Memnite
Ornithopter
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Tormod's Crypt
Island x19

